module gasd-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }

// The Southern District's own criminal periods and limits. In a
// multi-defendant case the government responds to all FRCrimP 12(b)(3)
// motions within fourteen days from the latest defendant's motion deadline
// (LR Crim. 12(a)(1)). A handwritten motion and brief, or response, is
// limited to twenty-five pages and a reply to ten (12(b)(2)), stated in
// pages, so it stays in this note. Failing to respond in time may result
// in the motion being granted without further notice (12(c)). Witness and
// exhibit lists are due at least three business days before a motion
// hearing (12(i)); business days have no engine lowering, so that period
// is a hole kept here. A response to a motion to continue is due within
// seven days, or sooner if the deadline, hearing or trial is earlier
// (12(j)). Discovery otherwise follows FRCrimP 16 and 26.2, Brady, Agurs,
// Giglio and the Jencks Act (16A). Objections to the draft presentence
// report are filed within fourteen days of its filing (32A(c)), FRCrimP
// 32(f)(1)'s own period, which stays with lit/frcrimp. In a revocation
// proceeding the government discloses its evidence at least seventy-two
// hours, and counsel confer at least forty-eight hours, before the final
// hearing (32.1(c), (d)); core's FRCrimP 45 counting rule does not admit
// hours (L3009), so those stay in this note. Criminal calendars follow the
// Speedy Trial Act and the court's plan (50); collateral forfeiture follows
// the court's schedule (58). The earlier outline's FRCrimP flow and its
// decisions belong to lit/frcrimp and are removed here: no reporter text
// is vendored.
/// A combined motion and brief, or a response: at most 6,500 words, and
/// filing certifies compliance (S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 12(b)(1)).
limit criminal-motion {
  words <= 6500 cite "S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 12(b)"
} cite "S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 12(b)"

/// A reply: at most 2,500 words (S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 12(b)(1)).
limit criminal-reply { words <= 2500 cite "S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 12(b)" } cite "S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 12(b)"

/// The defendant's arraignment (S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 12(a)(1), 16B(a)).
event Arraigned()
/// The last day for filing FRCrimP 12(b)(3) motions passes (S.D. Ga. LR
/// Crim. 12(a)(1)).
event MotionDeadlinePassed()
/// A pretrial motion is filed (S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 12).
event PretrialMotionFiled() paper criminal-motion
/// A response to a motion is filed (S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 12).
event MotionResponseFiled() paper criminal-motion
/// A reply on a motion is filed (S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 12(b)).
event MotionReplyFiled() paper criminal-reply
/// The government requests the defendant's FRCrimP 16(b)(1) disclosure
/// (S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 16D).
event GovernmentDisclosureRequested()
/// The date set for the pretrial conference, or for trial if none is held
/// (S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 16E(c)).
event PretrialConferenceScheduled()
/// The date set for trial (S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 16B(b), 16E(c), (d), 24(a)).
event TrialScheduled()
/// The date set for the sentencing hearing (S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 32A(d)).
event SentencingHearingScheduled()
/// The sentence is imposed (S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 32B(b)).
event Sentenced()
/// A motion for joint representation is filed (S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 44D(a)).
event JointRepresentationMotionFiled()
/// The Court denies a motion to seal (S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 49.1(d)).
event SealingDenied()

/// S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 12(a)(1): every pretrial motion described in FRCrimP
/// 12(b)(3) is filed within fourteen days from arraignment.
deadline pretrial-motion-period: 14.days after Arraigned() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 12(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 12(a)(1): responses to those motions are filed within
/// fourteen days of the last day for filing motions.
deadline pretrial-motion-response-period: 14.days after MotionDeadlinePassed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 12(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 12(a)(2): a response to any other pretrial motion is
/// filed within seven days of its filing, or as soon as possible if the
/// motion asks for relief sooner.
deadline other-motion-response-period: 7.days after PretrialMotionFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 12(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 16B(a): within fourteen days of arraignment, or
/// promptly after acquiring possession, the government discloses on request
/// the FRCrimP 16(a)(1) information, and Brady material, identification
/// procedures, vehicles, intercepts and grand jury transcripts.
deadline government-initial-disclosure-period: 14.days after Arraigned() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 16B(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 16B(b): no later than fourteen days before trial the
/// government discloses Giglio material and the general nature of prior or
/// intrinsic acts evidence.
deadline government-later-disclosure-period: 14.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 16B(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 16D: on the government's request, a defendant bound
/// by FRCrimP 16(b)(1) discloses not more than seven days after the request,
/// or promptly after acquiring possession.
deadline defense-disclosure-period: 7.days after GovernmentDisclosureRequested() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 16D"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 16E(c): at least seven days before the pretrial
/// conference, or with none seven days before trial, counsel confer on
/// stipulations of fact and of the authenticity or admissibility of
/// exhibits.
deadline stipulation-conference-period: 7.days before PretrialConferenceScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 16E(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 16E(c): the parties file all stipulations, signed by
/// the defendant, defense counsel and the government, at least two days
/// before trial.
deadline stipulation-filing-period: 2.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 16E(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 16E(d): demonstrative, summary and composite exhibits
/// (FRE 1006 included) are disclosed at least two days before trial.
deadline demonstrative-exhibit-period: 2.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 16E(d)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 24(a): unless ordered otherwise, requests for special
/// voir dire are filed no later than seven days before trial.
deadline voir-dire-request-period: 7.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 24(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 32A(d): unless the judge orders otherwise, a
/// sentencing memorandum on a complex sentencing issue is filed no later
/// than the day before the sentencing hearing.
deadline sentencing-memorandum-period: 1.days before SentencingHearingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite ?("S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 32A(d) states no later than the day prior to the sentencing hearing; the verifier treats LR Crim. 32A(c)'s separate 14-day objection period as if it applied to subsection (d), so this period remains unverified")
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 32B(b): defense counsel files the Post-Conviction
/// Consultation Certification, after explaining the appeal and the duty to
/// file one on request (32B(a)), no later than fourteen days after
/// sentencing.
deadline post-conviction-certification-period: 14.days after Sentenced() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 32B(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 44D(a): the government responds within seven days to
/// a motion for joint representation.
deadline joint-representation-response-period: 7.days after JointRepresentationMotionFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 44D(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 49.1(d): material a denied motion to seal sought to
/// seal is returned unless the movant files a notice of intent to appeal
/// the denial within fourteen days.
deadline sealing-appeal-notice-period: 14.days after SealingDenied() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Ga. LR Crim. 49.1(d)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}
